## Resolved mutable: chrome-row-cramming

Screenshot landing-desktop.png + browser-14: NOT chrome cramming. The catastrophic jank is .ds-section height=0 (all 7 main children collapse to height:0, content overlaps the hero). ROOT CAUSE (browser-15): kit .app-main is a FIXED-HEIGHT flex column (@media min-width:901px .app{height:100dvh;overflow:hidden}; .app-main{display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%;overflow-y:auto}) with .app-main>*{min-height:0}. Designed for app/dashboard routes (chat/file-stage fill viewport). For a long-scroll landing the flex children (.ds-section) shrink to min-height:0=0 because content exceeds the fixed container. Sections collapse, everything piles on the hero. The kit AppShell is the wrong shell altmode for a scrolling document — landing must make its .app-main children flex:0 0 auto (non-shrinking).